    <section>
      <p class="wide">
        Configure Simple Java Mail through its <strong>Java API</strong>, <strong>system properties</strong>, <strong>environment variables</strong>, or
        <strong>property files</strong>. The <a href="/spring.html">Spring integration</a> reads the same settings from Spring's environment.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section class="introduction">
    <div class="view">
      <p>
        The Java API and configuration files work together. A configuration snapshot resolves its sources in the order you list them, with later
        non-blank values winning. Calls on a builder then win over the snapshot values copied into that builder.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="side">
      <p>
        <strong>SimpleJavaMail</strong> is the application-level entry point. It gives you a fresh email or Mailer builder backed by one immutable
        configuration snapshot.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>ConfigLoader</strong> resolves an ordered set of sources into that snapshot. It has no process-wide registry, so separate factories can
        safely use different SMTP servers and message defaults in the same JVM.
      </p>
    </div>
    </section>

